=== PARITY (vs web UrlEncoder.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> useTranslation ONLY. The web source has NO data hooks (no Resource/query); it is a
    pure client-side transform. It is bound through the shared state-holder seam (UrlEncoderModel,
    P1/S8): the model owns mode+input and derives `result` exactly as the web `useMemo` does. The view
    performs NO transform logic and NO I/O. Because there is no async data source, the generic
    network states (loading/error/stale/offline) do NOT occur on this surface — this reproduces the
    source faithfully (it has none); it is not scope narrowing.
  Codec -> UrlEncoderCodec is a 1:1 port of encodeURIComponent / decodeURIComponent:
    encode percent-encodes every byte EXCEPT the JS unreserved set A-Z a-z 0-9 - _ . ! ~ * ' ( )
    (explicit ASCII set, NOT CharacterSet.alphanumerics, so non-ASCII emits UTF-8 triples:
    "café"->"caf%C3%A9", "世"->"%E4%B8%96; space/&/= -> %20/%26/%3D so the exact web example
    "hello world&foo=bar" -> "hello%20world%26foo%3Dbar"). decode returns .invalid on malformed
    escapes / invalid UTF-8 (the web try/catch -> t('Invalid Input')). Empty input -> .empty sentinel
    (web `if (!inputVal) return ''`). All verified by the executed XCTest (11 codec asserts).
  Composition -> ToolCard frame (link icon chip + "Url Encoder" title + "Url Encoder Desc") over a
    glass panel · Encode/Decode toggle (TSButton primary when active / ghost when inactive, mirroring
    the web variant switch) · "Input Label" + monospaced auto-growing input with the per-mode example
    prompt ("hello world&foo=bar" / "hello%20world%26foo%3Dbar", verbatim like the web) · output panel
    ("Output Label" + TSCopyButton + monospaced value, web `pre`).
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius + tsGlassPanel (web GlassPanel)
    + TSButton (web Button) + TSCopyButton (web CopyButton), compiled against the REAL apps/apple
    component library in the typecheck steps below. Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> empty (web hides the output panel; native shows a friendly hint, never a blank
    box) · value (output panel + copy) · invalid (web renders t('Invalid Input') in the panel with a
    copy button; native keeps the verbatim "Invalid Input" text but swaps copy for a danger-toned
    warning — the HIG-idiomatic error rendering the surface contract asks for; documented deviation).
    Each has a #if DEBUG preview; the empty/value/invalid branching is unit-tested + executed green.
  i18n -> every key the web source passes to t() resolves through the P1/S10 facade with the web
    fallback: "Url Encoder", "Url Encoder Desc", "Encode", "Decode", "Input Label", "Output Label",
    "Invalid Input" — ALL present in UrlEncoder.strings (values reproduce exactly what the web renders;
    the bare keys absent from en.json render as the key itself, Encode/Decode are identity in en.json).
    Plus 3 native chrome/a11y keys. No English literals in native code (verbatim from the facade).
  a11y -> icon decorative (hidden); title carries .isHeader; each toggle button has an accessibility
    label + .isSelected when active; the input has an explicit accessibilityLabel; the output carries a
    label + value; the invalid panel a combined danger label; Dynamic Type via the Font.TS ramp;
    no animation (no Reduce-Motion concern). The spoken output summary is a pure, unit-tested seam
    (UrlEncoderAccessibility.outputSummary).
  Telemetry -> UrlEncoderModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"UrlEncoder") -> bridges the shared
    Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test (fires exactly once).

